\**{c=red:Note:}** This Mission is optional and can be skipped by trading enough {p:Crystals|Crystal} to the {p:Conquest NPC}.
* Skipping this Mission has no impact on whether you get the 10% {p:Capacity Point bonus|Job Points} at Rank 10.

=2 Walkthrough
Trade enough {p:Crystals} (1+) to the {p:Conquest NPC} to raise your Rank bar and unlock the Mission, then accept it from the {n:Gate Guard}.
* Talk to any {n:Gate Guard} and accept the Mission.
** There are two in {z:Southern San d'Oria}, {n:Ambrotien} at (K-6) and {n:Endracion} at (F-9). There is also a gate guard in {z:Northern San d'Oria}, {n:Grilau} at (D-8).
* Buy a {@i:Crystal Bass|4528} {i:Crystal Bass|Crystal Bass|4528} from the {z:Auction House} ({@g:Auction House} > Food > Fish) or you can catch one in {z:Jugner Forest}.
** It is MUCH easier to buy one from the {z:Auction House}. Crystal Bass cap at 35 for fishing, so plan accordingly.
** See below for fishing tips.
* Trade the {i:Crystal Bass|Crystal Bass|4528} to the {n:Gate Guard}.
* Enter {z:Chateau d'Oraguille} for a cutscene.
* Talk to {n:Chalvatot} located in the late Queen Leaute's **Garden** by her Tombstone (F-7) inside {z:Chateau d'Oraguille} for a cutscene. Afterwards the Mission is completed.
** Repeating this Missions is similar to {M:Mission 1-2|San d'Oria Mission 1-2|Bat Hunt}. You do not need to zone between repeating, you also do not have to repeat the steps in {z:Chateau d'Oraguille}.

=2 Fishing for Crystal Bass
* Obtain Level 20 or higher.
** Characters less than 14 days old and below level 20 will experience {p:Fishing Fatigue|Category:Fishing}: after catching 10 fish in a day, you can not catch any more until the next day (midnight Japanese time). Otherwise your daily fishing limit is 200 fish.
** {m:Goblin Bounty Hunters|Goblin Bounty Hunter} patrol shorelines for low level players. Level 30s should be able to ignore them.
** Outside of cities, you can fish up monsters. There's a different message if there's a monster on your line. (More about fishing messages below)
* Fishing skill optional.
** Any fish involved in Missions (such as this one) or Quests can be caught with 0 skill unless otherwise specified like {q:Inside the Belly|Inside the Belly|Inside the Belly}.
** Fishing skill determines how many gold arrows appears in the mini-game, which wear out the fish's faster.
* Obtain a fishing rod and tackle:
** {@i:Carbon Fish. Rod|17384} {i:Carbon Fishing Rod|Carbon Fishing Rod|17384} or {@i:Halcyon Rod|17015} {i:Halcyon Rod|Halcyon Rod|17015} (craft with {p:Alchemy} or buy on {z:AH|Auction House}) are synthetic rods good for catching small fish.
*** These rods are some of the most durable non-legendary fishing rods and the line rarely breaks for any kind of small fish and items like {@i:Rusty Leggings|14117} {i:Rusty Leggings|Rusty Leggings|14117}.
** Alternatively, {@i:Bamboo Fish. Rod|17389} {i:Bamboo Fishing Rod|Bamboo Fishing Rod|17389} can be purchased in {z:Southern San d'Oria} from {n:Lusiane} (F-8) if San d'Oria is first place in {p:conquest|Conquest}.
*** It is a less durable rod, so it won't be as successful for reeling in items or certain fish (see specific fish pages for notes).
** **(Optional)** Obtain 1 {@i:Minnow|17407} {p:Minnow} (NPC buyable). It is a lure, does not stack.
** Obtain some {@i:Insect Ball|16998} {p:Insect Balls|Insect Ball}, they stack to 99. As much as you're comfortable with. These are good for early skill up and can catch Crystal Bass (while avoiding {i:Crayfish|Crayfish|4472} and {i:Red Terrapins|Red Terrapin|4402}). Use as a backup in case something takes your lure.
* **(Optional)** The mission requires 1 {i:Crystal Bass|Crystal Bass|4528}. However, there is another RoE objective for catching 10 Crystal Bass. Vana'versary -> 15th Vana'versary III -> {p:All That Glitters... (W)|Category:Records of Eminence}
* Go to {z:Jugner Forest} and find the Crystalwater Spring (J-9).
* Equip your fishing rod in the ranged slot. Bait goes in the ammo slot.
* Target yourself and use the Fishing action next to the water.
* Wait for the right fishing message.
** "Something caught the hook!" <- One exclamation point. It is a small fish. Reel it in.
** "Something caught the hook!!!" <- Three exclamation points. It is a "large fish". The {p:music|Category:Music} may change. There are no large fish in the crystal spring... that is a tree ({@i:Arrowwood Log|688} {i:Arrowwood Log|Arrowwood Log|688}). It will break your rod. Press Esc to let it go.
** "You feel something pulling at your line." <- Some rusty items. It's junk and you won't skill up either.
*** "You have a bad/terrible feeling about this one." <- This appears at the end of a message, hinting how likely something is hooked that will break your rod based on your fishing skill and rod's strength. It's probably trees. Press Esc to let it go.
** "Something clamps onto your line ferociously!" <- Monster. They don't drop crystal bass.

